WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.790
Welcome to the Microsoft for Education Daily, Monday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.510
Let's catch you up on everything new from Microsoft.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.460
One step at a time. The week's best opens with a slide tip for teachers.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.520
Reveal each point as you say it: students found it in about a second,

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.540
not almost six.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.470
In the study, they also remembered a little more,

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.160
though it was just 40 students.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.970
New on campus? A passkey can now be the first sign-in method you register,

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.830
rolling out through February.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.960
Windows Hello for Business, or a Mac's Platform single sign-on,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.420
now counts as multifactor on its own.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.670
Visiting researchers?

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.620
Stale guest accounts can be disabled automatically, in preview.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.330
Research teams? Kimi K3.1 Pro is in Foundry, with room for a million tokens.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.970
Media projects? Kling,

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:14.060
LTX and MiniMax video models are rolling out in Foundry, in public preview.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.630
Moving to Arm laptops?

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:22.180
GitHub Copilot's upgrade agent now helps port .NET apps to Windows on Arm.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.350
Idle AI agents? In preview, Entra warns owners after 60 days,

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.890
then disables those still idle.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.030
In calmer news,

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:37.240
Microsoft's paper finds Copilot Studio's new harness lifts pass rates by up to 22 points.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.450
When a step fails, they keep working up to 91% of the time, versus under 7%.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.650
The fine print? Still running Exchange Server on campus?

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:52.360
Emergency mitigations are due on by default in December.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.070
In Europe,

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:57.480
Claude in Copilot is due inside the EU Data Boundary by the end of the year.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.780
After hours?

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:08.720
Cat-Astrophy is out on Xbox: a space roguelite with freshly generated planets.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.980
No single right build here, and Star Fragments unlock upgrades for next time.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.230
And on November 13,

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:20.580
Where Winds Meet's Hutuo update brings Horse Racing Chess to Xbox.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.430
Reveal it piece by piece, start with a passkey,

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.680
tidy up guests: one step at a time.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.820
Every day, the changelog gets a little longer.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.800
Check the board: shipped today, and more on the way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.690
All of that, in one day. And it keeps on shipping.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.950
That's the Microsoft for Education Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.
